= 

*Question:*  Briefly describe one skill you brought to the negotiations that had a positive impact on the discussion. 

*Answer:* I suppose the skill of re-thinking things? I'm not too sure. I had us dig into the actual vibe we meant by the words we chose, because they seemed similar but we had very different interpretations. I'm not sure what else to really say here this was a pretty simple exercise? We didn't have to negotiate that much, we had an open conversation about the terms we chose and it was a pleasant time. Maybe there were skills involved I simply didn't notice?

= 

*Question:*  Briefly describe one thing you realized about your communication style that you will 
need to be aware of to keep it from having a negative impact on the discussion. 

*Answer:* I'm noticing I have a tendency to kind of run the conversation and also a tendency to overcorrect and walk back everything I'm saying. Finding the right balance of the two, knowing when to exert myself and when to simply listen, is going to be super important for navigating this project. I suppose I'm so used to being surrounded by people far more experienced than myself that I haven't had to think about this side of me in a while. I am normally so out of my depth that I don't have much to say, but here it's hard for me to stop talking. 



